# Lumen OS 1.0 memory tuning (install as /system/etc/init/z9x_speed.rc). Speed spec v7 section 5.
# Init builtins only (write): no exec, no service, nothing that can block or fail the boot.
# Runs at sys.boot_completed=1, i.e. after the vendor's init.fusion.rc 'on boot' writes
# (vm.swappiness 60, watermark_scale_factor 300).
#
# vm.swappiness [60 vendor] -> 100: prefer compressing idle anonymous pages into zram (hardware
# mzc_hybrid, ~7:1 on this device: mm_stat 530 MB stored in 76 MB) over dropping file pages (app
# code, .odex/.apk) that must then be re-read from eMMC on the next app switch.
# Rollback without a reflash: echo 60 > /proc/sys/vm/swappiness (root), or drop this line.
on property:sys.boot_completed=1
    write /proc/sys/vm/swappiness 100

# The lmkd values (ro.lmk.swap_free_low_percentage 10, thrashing_limit 30, psi_complete_stall_ms 700)
# and the ART thread props are in /product/etc/build.prop (lumen_v1.sh, product_prop_v1.txt); the
# cached-process cap (16) is in the framework RRO and the SimpleDeviceConfig RRO.
#
# [EXP E2, NOT active] watermark_scale_factor 385 keeps ~220 MB free at all times; 200 would keep
# ~115 MB. Ships only after 4K HDR + Kinopoisk DRM + YouTube 4K pass without dma-buf/ion allocation
# errors (speed spec 11 T8, with the user's approval on a test image).
# on property:sys.boot_completed=1
#     write /proc/sys/vm/watermark_scale_factor 200
